  "commonOk": "OK",
  "statusShockEffect": "Wider groups on every shot, less carried before it hurts, and above class III the picture dims and running makes you dizzy.",
  "statusShockFix": "Stop the bleeding first — a bandage or a tourniquet. Blood comes back on its own afterwards, slowly, and only if you eat and drink.",
  "statusShockWhere": "Pharmacies, clinics, ambulances; first-aid kits in offices and workshops.",
  "statusDehydratedEffect": "Hands go first: aim and reaction time. Deeper down it takes decisions, then strength.",
  "statusDehydratedFix": "Drink. It works over about twenty minutes, not instantly, so drink before you need it.",
  "statusDehydratedWhere": "Shops, petrol stations, homes. Water from a tap or a stream has to be boiled or treated first.",
  "statusStarvingEffect": "Everything takes longer — searching, bandaging, building — and precision goes with it.",
  "statusStarvingFix": "Eat. Tins and dry food keep; anything cooked is worth more per kilogram carried.",
  "statusStarvingWhere": "Shops, homes, restaurants, allotments. Bodies rarely carry more than a snack.",
  "statusSleepDeprivedEffect": "Every shot spreads wider, everything takes longer to learn, and past a day awake the eyes close on their own for a few seconds at a time.",
  "statusSleepDeprivedFix": "Sleep. Only sleep pays this down — and only somewhere safe enough to lie down, which means a shelter.",
  "statusSleepDeprivedWhere": "Your own shelter. A bed or a mattress makes the hours count for more.",
  "statusBleeding": "Bleeding",
  "statusDehydrated": "Dehydrated",
  "statusStarving": "Starving",
  "statusWasting": "Wasting",
  "statusWastingEffect": "Everything is slower and the hands are unsteady. Weaker than it looks on a full stomach.",
  "statusWastingFix": "Eat more than the day needs. It comes back slowly.",
  "statusWastingWhere": "Anything with calories in it. Tins keep.",
